---
// <GnnEdgeFigure> — one event through the edge classifier, on the neutrino page.
//
// Three panels: the raw hits on one wire plane, the kNN-8 cluster graph coloured
// by the network's merge probability, and the same graph carrying the truth
// labels. Read left to right it is the whole task: hits become Pandora cluster
// fragments, fragments become candidate edges, and the network decides which
// edges join fragments of the same particle.
//
// Unlike the event triptych, this is a COLOUR figure with axes and colourbars, so
// its white ground cannot be made transparent: the axis text would vanish in the
// dark view and the colourmaps would have to survive an inversion. It sits on a
// light plate in both themes instead, which is how a printed figure behaves.
//
// Source: MicroBooNE open data, v5 test event 273, CC νe. Made by the analysis in
// the group's gnn_merge study; delete the component and the page loses the figure.
const SRC = "/images/neutrino/gnn-edge-scores.png";
---

<figure class="gnn">
  <div class="gnn-plate">
    <img
      src={SRC}
      alt="Three panels for one simulated neutrino event. Left: 791 raw hits on one wire plane, coloured by charge. Centre: the kNN-8 cluster graph with each candidate edge coloured by the network's merge probability, blue for low and red for high. Right: the same graph with the true labels, 601 edges joining fragments of the same particle and 309 joining different particles."
      width="1700"
      height="567"
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async"
    />
  </div>
  <figcaption class="gnn-caption">
    One event through the edge classifier. Hits are grouped into Pandora cluster
    fragments, and the network scores every candidate edge between them; on this
    view it reaches an edge F1 of 0.91. MicroBooNE open data, a CC νe test event.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .gnn {
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 0;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  /* A light plate in both themes. The figure carries its own axes, labels and
     colourbars, so it is read as a printed plate rather than as ink on the card. */
  .gnn-plate {
    background: #fff;
    border: var(--hairline) solid var(--border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    padding: var(--space-2);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .gnn-plate img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    /* Three wide panels: below this the detail is unreadable, so it scrolls. */
    min-width: 520px;
  }
  .gnn-caption {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
</style>
